      "body": "## Summary\n\nFix two related shutdown ownership bugs in CPU KV offload.\n\n### 1. Shared handler reference lists\n\nBefore this change, the store and load handlers received the same mutable\n`cpu_tensors` list. When one handler cleared its tensor references during\nshutdown, it also cleared the other handler's list. This alias existed for\nboth shared-region and private-tensor paths.\n\nEach handler now owns its own reference container. The tensor objects and\ntheir backing storage are not copied.\n\n### 2. Private tensor lifetime after shutdown failure\n\nWhen `mmap_region=None`, the worker uses private CPU tensors and has no shared\nregion object as an independent backing-memory owner. The existing device-wide\nsynchronization was only attempted inside the shared-region cleanup branch.\nIf a handler failed to synchronize an end event, private tensor references\ncould be released before outstanding accelerator work was known to be complete.\n\nThe worker now retains an independent owner for private CPU tensors and only\nreleases it after handler shutdown and any required accelerator synchronization\ncomplete successfully.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Give each `SingleDirectionOffloadingHandler` its own tensor-reference lists.\n- Keep worker-owned private CPU tensors alive through handler shutdown.\n- Synchronize the current accelerator after either handler reports a shutdown\n  failure, regardless of whether a shared mmap region is used.\n- Preserve the existing shared-region cleanup order.\n\n## Relationship to existing PRs\n\n- Related context: #57160 changed ROCm CPU KV offload to use private pinned\n  tensors after shared mmap registration failures. It made the private path\n  more visible but did not introduce these generic ownership issues.\n- Related but distinct: #53073 fixes shared mmap-region ownership and startup\n  cleanup. This PR fixes handler reference ownership and private buffer lifetime\n  during asynchronous shutdown.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe existing behavior after a shared-region device synchronization failure is\nunchanged and is outside this PR's scope.\n\n## Tests\n\n```text\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/v1/kv_offload/cpu/test_gpu_worker.py -q\n42 passed, 1 skipped\n\n.venv/bin/pre-commit run --files \\\n  vllm/v1/kv_offload/cpu/gpu_worker.py \\\n  tests/v1/kv_offload/cpu/test_gpu_worker.py\npassed\n```\n\nThe tests validate generic CPU/mock ownership and shutdown behavior. No\naccelerator hardware validation was available in this environment.\n\nNo model evaluation is required because this change does not affect model\noutputs, accuracy, or serving behavior.\n\nAI assistance was used to prepare this change. The human submitter must review\nevery changed line and be able to explain the ownership and shutdown semantics\nbefore submission.\n",
